  "logline": "Forty years ago, safecracker Dot Kowalczyk hid the one thing she ever stole for love inside the vault of the bank that framed her crew. Now the bank is being demolished — so the surviving members of the Marlowe Street gang, average age seventy-eight, are going back in to get it.",
  "tagline": "One last job. Nap permitting.",
  "synopsis": "The Marlowe Street crew were never caught, because their one important job was never reported. In 1984 they lifted a corrupt developer's strongbox, and safecracker Dot Kowalczyk hid its irreplaceable contents — love letters that clear her late husband's name — inside the First Mercantile vault wall during the getaway. Now the Mercantile is demolished in sixty days, and Dot, eighty-one, reassembles the crew: getaway driver Sal, whose license and eyesight are both negotiable; forger Miriam, now the parish calligrapher, who denies nothing; and Eddie, the inside man, who took a janitor's job at the bank in 1985 as cover and simply never left. The plan must work around medications, hearing aids, and a security system installed by Dot's grandson. What they are stealing is worthless to everyone else on Earth — exactly why four old thieves will risk their only remaining asset, their legend, to steal it back.",
  "characters": [
   {
    "name": "Dot Kowalczyk",
    "role": "Retired safecracker and crew leader, 81",
    "note": "She cracked the Mercantile in eleven minutes in 1984 and has opened nothing more dangerous than jars since. Her motivation is a promise to a dead man: the letters prove her husband died innocent, and she intends to keep her word before the wrecking ball keeps its appointment."
   },
   {
    "name": "Salvatore 'Sal' Benedetti",
    "role": "Getaway driver, 79",
    "note": "Once the finest wheelman on the East Coast, now forbidden by his cardiologist from excitement of any kind. He joins the job because retirement has taught him that a quiet life and a pointless one feel identical, and he refuses to die of the second."
   },
   {
    "name": "Miriam Okafor",
    "role": "Forger, 77",
    "note": "A church calligrapher whose hand once moved money across three continents. She has made a good life and a clean conscience and joins the crew anyway, because Miriam has never once, in seventy-seven years, been able to resist a signature that needed her."
   },
   {
    "name": "Eddie Vance",
    "role": "Inside man, bank janitor, 80",
    "note": "He took the janitor's job in 1985 as cover for one night and simply never left, becoming the bank's beloved institution. Eddie knows every camera, every guard's grandchild and every vent — and that demolishing the building means demolishing the only life he built out of the worst night of it."
   }
  ],
