  "logline": "At 11:53 p.m., dispatcher Mara Quinn takes a mayday from Meridian Flight 217 — the plane that crashed into the Atlantic ten years ago tonight, with her husband at the controls.",
  "tagline": "The crash already happened. Answer anyway.",
  "synopsis": "Mara Quinn, 38, has worked the graveyard shift at a regional emergency dispatch center for a decade, ever since Meridian Flight 217 crashed and made her a widow. At 11:53 p.m. on the crash's tenth anniversary, her console lights up with a distress call using 217's call sign, its captain's voice, and a fuel emergency unfolding in real time. Her supervisors call it a hoax or a system ghost. But the caller knows the cargo manifest that was never made public, and describes weather matching tonight, not 2015. While federal agents move to shut her down and a storm closes over the same stretch of Atlantic, Mara gets seven minutes of radio contact at a time to work out whether she is being played, haunted, or given what no investigator ever got: a second chance to land that plane.",
