  "logline": "In Lumen, a city where the lights never go out and shadows are illegal, a crime-scene photographer develops a picture containing a shadow that should not exist — cast by a door that opens downward.",
  "tagline": "Darkness was outlawed. It went underground.",
  "synopsis": "Fifty years after the Blackout Riots, the city of Lumen burns with permanent artificial daylight. Sleep is medicated, night is treason, and shadows — proof of unregistered darkness — are a criminal offense. Vera Lindqvist, 36, photographs crime scenes for the Illumination Authority and prides herself on seeing everything. Then one of her exposures develops wrong: a long shadow, in a sealed white room, falling from a door that exists in no plan of the building. Following it costs Vera her license, her apartment's light ration, and her name on the citizen register. Below the flooded maintenance levels she finds the Umbral — thousands living in true darkness: growing food, raising children who have never seen the sun, and keeping the one secret Lumen's founders killed to bury. Vera must choose which city gets her photograph, knowing publication means a war between light and dark.",
