  "tagline": "The empire ends. The road does not.",
  "synopsis": "In the summer of 476 AD, the Western Roman Empire is a rumor maintained by courier routes. Flavius Corvus, 29, a third-generation imperial messenger of Gothic descent, is given the last sealed dispatch of the Emperor Romulus: an order recalling the eastern legions to defend Ravenna. Every power on the peninsula wants the seal unbroken and the rider dead, bribed or turned — the Gothic commander Odoacer, offering Corvus what Rome never gave his family, citizenship and land; a bishop quietly building the church into the state that will replace the empire; and Corvus's own brother, riding for the other side. Across one summer of burned bridges, plague villages and armies that exist mostly on paper, Corvus must decide what a message is worth when the world that sent it is already gone.",
