  "logline": "Night-train conductor Ruth Adler counts eleven passengers in coach four every night — twelve on the security feed. The twelfth man always sits in seat 9, always faces the camera, and tonight he is holding her lost brother's coat.",
  "tagline": "He only exists when watched.",
  "synopsis": "Ruth Adler, 52, has worked the overnight Vienna-Venice train for nineteen years and runs her coaches by count: tickets, heads, cameras, every night. For six weeks the counts have disagreed. Coach four's cameras show a man in seat 9 — gray coat, still hands, face never resolved — whom Ruth has never seen standing in the aisle. Security calls it a compression artifact; her supervisor suggests sleep. Ruth begins an experiment log, and the artifact responds: he changes seats to sit nearer her office, appears on a camera that was not recording, and one night leaves, visible only on playback, a folded timetable from 2004 — the year her brother Daniel boarded a train on this route and never arrived anywhere. Ruth must decide whether she is being haunted, surveilled, or broken by grief, before the night the feed shows seat 9 empty and her own office door opening.",
